4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Definition, diabetes is an error of glucose metabolism.

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.000
You don't metabolize your glucose well. That's what diabetes is.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.000
You cannot metabolize glucose for whatever reason.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Sometimes it's a lack of insulin. Sometimes the cells become resistant to insulin.

8
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.000
For whatever reason, you cannot metabolize glucose.

9
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Now the problem with glucose is it's your primary fuel source.

10
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:48.000
So diabetes get into trouble because they can't metabolize or use the primary fuel source.

11
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
And without that, cells die. And that's why it's very bad.

12
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Now don't confuse it with diabetes insipidus because diabetes insipidus is a totally different disease.

13
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Diabetes insipidus is not a type of diabetes mellitus. It's a totally different disease.

14
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Diabetes, in the parenthesis, I want you to put diabetes insipidus is polyuria, polydipsia,

15
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:37.000
leading to dehydration due to low ADH.

16
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:44.000
So when you get a question about diabetes insipidus and they want to know what you see,

17
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:54.000
what do you see? Polyuria, polydipsia, and dehydration, which looks a lot like diabetes mellitus, doesn't it?

18
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Because it has polyuria, polydipsia, and dehydration.

19
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:07.000
So they look alike even though they're not the same thing. That's why they share the same first name, diabetes.

20
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:17.000
So if you're sitting there and you can't remember what diabetes insipidus is, what's the best way to remember?

21
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:28.000
It's like diabetes mellitus only just with the fluids. It's just the fluid part of diabetes mellitus.

22
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.000
You don't get the glucose part. You just get the fluid part. And it's due to a low ADH.

23
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:42.000
So what they'll ask you about diabetes insipidus is, a lot of times with diabetes insipidus, what they would ask you is, do you have a low urine output or a high urine output?

